<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88112" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προνώπια</span></b> , τά, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>front of a house</i> (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνώπια</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἐς προνώπι᾽ αὐτίχ᾽ ἥξει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					639
				</span></i>
			 (troch.): metaph. in sg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόδ᾽
				ἔσχατον . . χώρας Πελοπίας π.,</span> of Troezen, the
			outer <i>portal</i> of Peloponnesus, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				374
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶς προνώπιος φαίνῃ πρὸς οἴκοις . .;</span>”
				<i>in front, before the door,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					645
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥρωες π.,</span>
			=
			<i>Lares compitales,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				4.14
			</span></i>. (Acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρό, ἐνώπια,</span> i.e.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πρὸ τῶν ἐνωπίων</span>: but the
			etym. is doubtful.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
